From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs: CreateImageEncoder writes Direct2D images (6045)

IWICImagingFactory2::CreateImageEncoder gave E_NOTIMPL, so a program could
not save what it drew with Direct2D through WIC. The image encoder draws
the image on its device into a bitmap of its own (all of a bitmap, the
area WICImageParameters name, or another image's bounds), reads it back
and writes it to the frame, or sets it as the frame's or encoder's
thumbnail, as a WIC bitmap the frame converts to its own format.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windowscodecs/Makefile.in b/dlls/windowscodecs/Makefile.in
index 511d451..da127fe 100644
--- a/dlls/windowscodecs/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/windowscodecs/Makefile.in
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ SOURCES = \
 	fliprotate.c \
 	gifformat.c \
 	icoformat.c \
+	imageencoder.c \
 	imgfactory.c \
 	info.c \
 	libjpeg.c \
diff --git a/dlls/windowscodecs/imageencoder.c b/dlls/windowscodecs/imageencoder.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5d9a8af
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/windowscodecs/imageencoder.c
@@ -0,0 +1,293 @@
